WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.460
Since their first appearance in a 1982 issue
of Peter Parker, the Spectacular Spider-Man,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.640
the mysterious heroes known as Cloak and Dagger
have captivated Marvel's true believers.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.000
Their unique and complementary powers, along
with an intriguing backstory and a compelling

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.260
romantic angle, made them fan favorites long
before they hit TV.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.840
But while everybody knows about Spider-Man,
fewer know the finer details of this relatively

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.020
obscure, co-dependent superhero duo.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.920
If you're in the dark, we'll shine a light
on the untold truth of Cloak and Dagger.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.540
D.A.R.E. to be a hero

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.480
The origin stories for Cloak and Dagger are
among the darker tales in Spider-Man's corner

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.540
of Marvel Comics.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.570
The first Cloak and Dagger story saw teenage
runaways Tyrone Johnson and Tandy Bowen kidnapped

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.460
by a mob chemist and experimented on with
synthetic heroin.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.660
They weren't the first runaways to be subjected
to the experiment, but they were the first

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.000
to survive, finding themselves after their
escape to be blessed and cursed with bizarre

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:52.500
powers.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.900
Cloak is able to banish people to the "Dark
Dimension" through a portal within his cloak,

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.300
while Dagger produces shards of solid light
which can be used as weapons.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.820
Sealing their partnership, Dagger also uses
her powers to provide Cloak with spiritual

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:09.350
sustenance, battling back a constant hunger
for life energy that he feels as an embodiment

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.080
of darkness.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.660
If not for her light, Cloak would need to
sustain himself with other living beings — not

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.800
an ideal situation.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.080
In their first 4-issue series in 1983, the
duo worked together as a team sworn to end

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:21.880
the drug trade.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:26.000
With their origin story steeped in dramatic
drug abuse, plus Cloak's addictive need for

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:30.751
Dagger's light, it's easy to read the duo
as a Reagan-era metaphor for drug abuse and

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:31.720
the war on narcotics.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.680
Considering how much opiate use in America
has increased since the time they were introduced,

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:40.520
it's not a plot that's aged well — to a
modern reader, their original mission mostly

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:41.380
just looks quaint.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.680
"So yes to your life, and when it comes to
drugs and alcohol, Just say no."

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.500
Mantlo's Marvel

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.380
Writer Bill Mantlo is one of the quirkier
storytellers in Marvel history, the creator

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.820
of Cloak, Dagger, and also Rocket Raccoon.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:01.220
He worked on Marvel's toy tie-in titles like
ROM: Spaceknight and Micronauts before being

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.030
assigned to write for more popular titles
like The Incredible Hulk and Peter Parker,

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.460
the Spectacular Spider-Man.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.620
He conceived Cloak and Dagger as supporting
characters for the Peter Parker series, saying

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:14.690
that the duo's backstory and abilities came
to him fully-formed during a trip to Ellis

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.190
Island.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.440
According to Mantlo's personal essay on the
characters, the pair embodied the feelings

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.280
that he felt there:

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.400
“They came in the night, when all was silent
and my mind was blank.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.280
They came completely conceived as to their
powers and attributes, their origin and motivation.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.920
They embodied between them all that fear and
misery, hunger and longing that had haunted

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.940
me on Ellis Island.”

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.000
The story Mantlo put together after his trip
was his first submission for Spectacular Spider-Man,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.640
and it was also, he felt, the best story he'd
ever written.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.660
Friendly neighbors of Spider-Man

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.000
After they escaped from death by overdose,
Cloak and Dagger made it their mission to

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.080
seek deadly vengeance.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:52.860
They were successful, despite the attempted
interference of the Friendly Neighborhood

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.080
Wall-Crawler, who generally frowns on the
use of deadly force.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.780
While the duo were merciless and single-minded
in this first appearance, yet also young and

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.960
naïve, qualities the sympathetic Spider-Man
understood all too well, making their turn

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.690
as a pair of Spider-Man antagonists extremely
brief.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.860
"What I'm trying to say is, superhero team-up?

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.780
Thanks in part to Spidey's friendship, the
wayward duo soon backed off from their ruthless

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:18.760
ways — a little tougher for Cloak, what
with the need to consume living beings and

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.260
all.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.720
With the duo's introductory arc being successful,
Cloak and Dagger were soon spun off of the

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.100
pages of Spider-Man to headline a series of
their own.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:27.920
Strange bedfellows

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:33.570
Between 1987 and '88, Cloak and Dagger's stories
were combined with Doctor Strange's in the

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.940
pages of one series, Strange Tales.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:40.551
The combined title was made as an effort to
boost sales for both series, but oddly, Strange

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.800
Tales didn't see the young heroes teaming
up with the Sorcerer Supreme.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:48.530
Instead, each issue featured a Cloak and Dagger
story with its own writing and art staff,

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:52.180
followed by a Doctor Strange story from its
own separate creative team.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.040
Basically, it was two comics in one.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:58.760
Previous Cloak and Dagger stories had been
extremely light on supervillains, mainly using

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.060
run-of-the-mill drug dealers and street criminals
for its antagonists.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.460
But Strange Tales started to flesh out a more
proper rogues' gallery for the pair, including

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:09.660
the demon Nightmare and the powerful magician
Mister Jip.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.680
The combo book served its purpose in keeping
both Cloak and Dagger and Doctor Strange above

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.340
water in popular consciousness.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.591
Cloak and Dagger split after issue 18 and
started their own title, while Doctor Strange

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.460
got his own title after 19 issues, ending
the series.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.280
The new mutates

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:30.260
A new comic series called The Mutant Misadventures
of Cloak and Dagger debuted in 1988, and its

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.740
title inadvertently contributed to a debate
that would go on for years.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:37.800
The question of whether Cloak and Dagger are
mutants went back and forth among comic fans

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.880
for decades, and a proper answer was only
recently offered.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:44.800
The question of whether the experimental drug
that gave the heroes their powers worked by

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.780
triggering latent mutant abilities was muddled
for years.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:51.900
Mutant Misadventures seemed to clear it up
with its title alone, and it was mentioned

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:55.910
more than once in the first issue that it
was indeed latent mutant genes that allowed

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:58.380
them to survive the experiment and gave them
their powers.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:03.500
But in a 2010 Cloak and Dagger one-shot, they
submit to extensive DNA testing—and are

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:07.920
shocked to discover that neither of them carry
mutant DNA, and that it was the experimental

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.360
drug and their own suffering that made them
what they are.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.980
No matter how you slice it, that's pretty
potent stuff.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.360
The teen angst Achilles heel

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.000
Cloak and Dagger are a formidable duo, but
if they have one glaring weakness, it's how

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.680
vulnerable they are to having their heads
screwed with.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.200
As teenage runaways granted awesome powers,
they're both pretty easily manipulated — but

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.480
Cloak in particular is kind of a pushover.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.380
Powerful beings have a tendency to try to
take control of his power for themselves,

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:37.780
with varying degrees of success ranging from
"Dagger has to talk him down" to "super-team

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.930
should probably intervene."

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.660
"Dear Diary, My teen angst b------- has a
body count"

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:49.100
Notably, the dream demon Nightmare has targeted
Cloak twice, overwhelming him with darkness

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.540
and taking him under control.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:54.720
The pair's emotional instability and codependency
are their biggest weaknesses.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:58.140
They may be tough to overpower in a fight,
but exploiting their teen angst has been an

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:00.020
effective strategy for many foes.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:01.960
Born from despair

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.520
As it turns out, this was no ordinary experimental
drug.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.580
It was created with the help of a demonic
being named D'Spayre who feeds on human pain

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.400
and suffering through a the spread of an insidious,
addictive drug called D-Lite.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.020
At the end of their 19-issue 1990 series,
the demon revealed to the duo that he helped

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.120
create them, imbuing Dagger and Cloak with
the light and dark sides of his own power.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:26.230
Bizarrely, that made them both weaker and
also made them swap their powers.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.920
He had intended to use them as sort of misery
batteries, soaking up their pain to feed on

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:31.640
at his leisure.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.980
His identity and motives are perfectly fitting
for the characters, with their greatest nemesis

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:39.020
turning out to be the living embodiment of
their own teenage angst.

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:41.760
Why he looks so much like Skeletor, though?

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:42.920
Your guess is as good as ours.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.380
"haha"

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:47.800
Thanks for watching!

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.220
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
